      "title": "Generac Q3 Earnings Beat Estimates on C&I Strength, Revenues Miss",
      "summary": "Generac Holdings reported Q3 2026 adjusted EPS of $2.54, beating estimates by 6.7%, with earnings up 38.8% year-over-year. While revenues missed expectations at $1.29B, the company's Commercial & Industrial segment surged 28% driven by data center demand, with backlog reaching $4.5B. A major $2.4B long-term supply agreement with Amazon for backup power generators in 2027-2028 significantly boosts growth visibility. Generac raised its 2026 EBITDA margin guidance and maintained full-year sales outlook.",
